  "question": {
    "text": "Experimentally reducing a functional group <strong>cannot</strong> be done by which one of the following reagents ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pt</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pd</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Sodium reacts with Hydrogen to form sodium hydride.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Na</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NaH</mi></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;cannot be used for reduction of functional groups.</p><p>All other reagents are used as reducing agent.</p>"
  }
